{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>According to all that you asked, etc.</b> Scripture does not complete here the request that they asked, for in saying \"I will not continue to hear the voice of YHWH\" (Deuteronomy 5:24) they would not be worthy of prophets. But when they said (Deuteronomy 5:24) \"You approach and hear all that YHWH our Elohim will speak, and you shall speak to us all that YHWH our Elohim speaks to you, and we will hear and we will do\" — then they accepted to believe in His prophets and to hear and to do all that HaShem commands through them. Therefore He says here: \"A prophet from among you, from your brothers, like me — HaShem will raise up for you,\" and you shall believe in him just as you believe in me, for thus you asked that the words of HaShem be with you through me and that you hearken to me; if so, believe also in the rest of the prophets who come after me, for those like me are like them. And this is the meaning of \"they spoke well\" — to believe in My prophets, \"and so I will do for them for their generations.\" And it is possible that their request there was for all generations, and their acceptance, when they said they would hear from Moses — \"and you shall speak to us and we will hear and we will do\" — was likewise for all generations. And the meaning of <b>and you (ואת)</b> will be: \"and you and every prophet of HaShem like you,\" as I explained there."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "In the final paragraph, Ramban's reading of ואת as elliptical for 'and you and every prophet...' follows his interpretation on Deuteronomy 5:24, there cross-referenced by 'as I explained there.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:51:44.951681712Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}